97
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
He said two popular ideas in the tech

98
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
and the startup worlds are:

99
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
failing fast and minimum viable project.

100
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
I believe both of these can be applied to scouting.

101
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
We don't expect scouts to start learning

102
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
how to build a fire with a big, giant, elaborate fire.

103
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
We want them to concentrate on the basics

104
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
of gathering what they need to build the fire.

105
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
The minimum viable project-

106
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
As fun as fire building- is the organizational skills

107
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
to put everything together and get the fire lit.

108
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
and burning doesn't come easy to scouts.

109
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
We want them to fail fast

110
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
and learn what they've done

111
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
and try again to their success.

112
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Again, I agree:

113
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Failing fast and the minimum viable project

114
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
is a good concept for scouts,

115
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
because we want them in that loop as quickly as possible.

116
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
We don't need to over explain,

117
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
We don't need to over instruct.

118
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Let them get at it, That's the whole thing.

119
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Let them be active, Let them fail fast,

120
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Let them produce, you know,

121
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
kind of a minimal product to begin with,

122
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
